Subject: [PATCH] hyprvx: seat-local pointer coordinates, constraints and warps
 through the camera

Patch 0007 of the HyprVX V3 series (Feature 001, Phase 2, T062).

mouseMoveUnified computes the pointer in window-content (world)
coordinates once (screenToWorld, monitor by screen position) and uses it
wherever a window-content position is subtracted: the fallback local
(forced focus, X11, held-button focus, seat grab), the main-surface box
check and sendMotionEventsToFocused. Layer, lock and IME surfaces keep
screen coordinates (isWindowContent).

Pointer constraints of window content: the confine region and the lock
hint are world positions; the closest point is found in world space and
the cursor is warped to its screen image (cammath::forward).
CWindow::warpCursor and the persistent-warp bookkeeping, and the
off-window axis clamp/warp, use the same conversions.
---
 src/config/shared/actions/ConfigActions.cpp |  5 ++-
 src/desktop/view/Window.cpp                 | 10 ++++--
 src/managers/input/InputManager.cpp         | 37 ++++++++++++++-------
 3 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

